> macro-op is when x86 decoder parses instruction queue and sees CISC instructions that can be fused together
  e.g., fuse cmp and jne [target]
  So decoder will decode both of these two instructions in unison. Effectively it increases the decoded instructions
  per cycle count

> micro-op fusion is when decoder takes a single CISC instruction and fuses some of the resultant u-ops together
  for more efficient downstream scheduling. This can hurt concurrency and or induce pipeline delays.
  e.g., add [mem], reg
  load-op-add and store are two separate u-ops

